The code clearly shows the bug. In `frame()`, when a collision is detected:
```javascript
    if (collides(state.ball, brick)) {
      brick.alive = false;
      state.combo += 1;
      state.score += scoreForBrick(brick, state.combo);
      // BUG (#1): the ball is NOT deflected here. Only the walls and the paddle
      // bounce (in step()); bricks were never given a bounce. So the ball plows
      // straight through a column head-on AND straight through the side of a
      // row. Fix = a real per-face bounce (flip vy on a top/bottom hit, vx on a
      // side hit) plus pushing the ball back out of the brick.
    }
```
The brick is marked as dead, but the ball's velocity is not changed. This means the ball continues its trajectory. If there's another brick behind it, it will just kill that one too. If the ball is moving fast or the bricks are thick (not the case here, but for later), it might skip over them.

However, since the ball is not deflected, it "plows straight through".

